## 1. Executive summary — the five biggest wins

1. **Finish the #996 rAF coalescing everywhere** — migrate the ~55 remaining audio/meter card loops **and** the 29 video-preview present loops (full-res GL blit + drawImage sync each frame, zero off-screen gating) onto the shared `onMeterFrame` ticker. Single largest remaining slice of the SHOES1 main-thread contention → output-underrun class. [V / P0]
2. **Split the 5 MB boot mega-chunk** — `/` ships 1.96 MB compressed JS (one 1.45 MB-br chunk: all 191 cards + 271 defs + doc prose, eagerly globbed) before ANY pixel or sound. Lazy per-card imports + docs-prose dedupe target boot < 700 KB compressed. [V / P0]
3. **Actually terminate AudioWorklet processors on module delete** — 0 of 69 processors ever `return false`, Faust `destroy()` has zero call sites; every delete/preset-slot cycle permanently accumulates live processors on the render thread. Monotonic render-budget drain compounding the underrun class. [U / P0]
4. ~~**Kill the per-Yjs-update full-graph cascade**~~ **← DONE, #1031 (2026-07-06).** Every doc update synchronously rebuilt the whole snapshot, handed xyflow all-new flowNodes/flowEdges identities, re-walked the reconciler, and fanned out to per-card `ydoc.on('update')` observers doing O(E) proxy walks. All three seams of P1-6 shipped; the #719 memoization TODO is closed. [V(partial)/U / P1]
5. **Make underruns visible and self-mitigating** — zero runtime underrun detection today (grep `renderCapacity|playoutStats` = 0) with a Tight-12 ms default; add the detector + "switch to Stable" nudge + an audio-first video frame governor (video halves to 30 fps under audio pressure). [V / P1]

