#### P0-1 · Finish the rAF coalescing program: ALL remaining per-card loops onto `onMeterFrame` [V — audio#1 P0, video#1+mainthread#1 (U), mainthread#6, stability#5]
- **What:** Mechanically migrate every remaining self-rescheduling card rAF onto the shared ticker, classifying each loop: **paint-only** → `onMeterFrame(cardEl, draw)` (visibility-gated); **stateful** (input polls, WASM pumps, capture, engine→store sync) → `onMeterFrame(null, cb)` (never gated). Three populations:
  - ~55 audio/meter/playhead card loops (e.g. AnalogVco, GraphicEq, Sequencer, Moog960, Spectrograph, Score, Writeseq, Cartesian, Featurecv, Twotracks, Clipplayer; KriaCard leftover loop at KriaCard.svelte:214-226 — 2-line fix, it already imports the ticker).
  - 29 video-preview present loops doing `videoEngine.blitOutputToDrawingBuffer(id)` (full-res pass, engine.ts:1033-1055) + `ctx2d.drawImage(engine.canvas)` (a GPU pipeline sync) per frame with **zero** IntersectionObserver adoption (VideoOutCard.svelte:107,213-272; BackdraftCard.svelte:245-291; Milkdrop, Recorderbox, Toybox, B3ntb0x, …). An off-screen video card today still costs a full-res blit + GL sync every frame.
  - Split-outs that must NOT be gated: BackdraftCard.svelte:289 `syncMirrorFromEngine`, RecorderboxCard capture drawImage + `recorder.frame()` (:207-242), Gamepad/Doom/game polls (Doom’s loop includes a 1 MB BGRA swap + putImageData). Also delete the busy-poll retry branches (e.g. GraphicEqCard.svelte:100-113) — the ticker re-invokes next frame.
- **Evidence:** meter-frame.ts:86-103; forensics plan §2 C1#2 ("63 per-card rAF loops" = the underrun driver); PR #996 body defers "~50 cards fast-follow"; Fix-E plan §3 names the per-card present sync "a separate, cheaper win" (unparked).
- **Expected win:** N−1 rAF callbacks/frame; ALL present/paint work stops for off-screen cards; for video cards this also removes N full-res GL syncs/frame when scrolled away. Direct reduction of the measured underrun surface.
- **Effort:** M (mechanical, wide). ~6 batches of ~10 cards/PR.
- **Risk + gates:** Mis-classifying a stateful loop as paint-only silently breaks off-screen behavior (recordings drop frames, gamepads stop calibrating, games pause) — classification review per card. VRT should be paint-identical (driver changes, not paint code) — run `task vrt` per batch and inspect; flake-check animated cards 3×; no ART/attest churn (cards are lib/ui, not in any attest basis). ~29-file video diff will conflict with in-flight card PRs — sweep after each merge.
- **Measure:** Headed-Chrome longtask counter (forensics plan §3-D) + count rAF callbacks/frame via a debug counter in the ticker, on a 20-card mixed patch, before/after each batch; DevTools Performance trace main-thread self-time of `Animation Frame Fired`.

